@startuml openplc-fbd-prompt-activity-diagram
!theme plain
title OpenPLC Function Block Diagram Generation - Prompt Activity Workflow\nSequential Execution of 10 Prompt Steps

start

:Input: Control Narrative +\nContext Generation Output;
note right
  Contains:
  - Original control narrative
  - Identified sensor types
  - Identified actuator types  
  - Selected control strategy
  - BASIC_LIB specifications
end note

:Execute Prompt 1\n**openplc-function-blocks-v2**\nAnalyze specification to identify\nall required function blocks;
note right
  Output: Function Blocks list
  Focus: Sensors, transmitters,
  actuators, controllers
end note

:Execute Prompt 2\n**openplc-function-blocks-validation**\nValidate and update function block list\nfor completeness against specifications;
note right
  Input: Original specification +
  Function blocks from Step 1
  Output: Validated function blocks
  Focus: Cross-reference tagnames
end note

:Execute Prompt 3\n**openplc-block-connections-and-logic**\nCreate connections and logic functions\nfor main control strategy only;
note right
  Input: Original specification +
  Validated function blocks
  Output: Functions + Block connections
  Focus: Main control logic only
end note

:Execute Prompt 4\n**openplc-block-connections-interlocks**\nImplement interlock and alarm logic\nwith boolean functions and connections;
note right
  Input: Original specification +
  Function blocks + Data connections
  Output: Interlock functions + connections
  Focus: Safety systems and alarms
end note

:Execute Prompt 5\n**openplc-parameter-data-connections**\nIdentify specific parameter values\nfor function blocks and functions;
note right
  Input: Original specification +
  Function blocks + Functions/connections
  Output: Parameter data connections
  Focus: Configuration values, setpoints
end note

:Execute Prompt 6\n**openplc-input-variables-and-connections**\nUpdate and refine parameter data\nconnections for full coverage;
note right
  Input: Original specification +
  Function blocks + Connections +
  Parameter data connections
  Output: Complete parameter connections
  Focus: Ranges, alarm limits
end note

:Execute Prompt 7\n**openplc-output-variables-and-connections**\nCreate output variables and connections\nfor system interfacing;
note right
  Input: Original specification +
  Function blocks from Step 2
  Output: Output variables + connections
  Focus: Monitoring points, interfaces
end note

:Execute Prompt 8\n**openplc-rule-checks**\nPerform comprehensive validation\nand consolidate all connections;
note right
  Input: Original specification +
  All outputs from Steps 2,3,4,6,7
  Output: Validated consolidated FBD
  Focus: IEC 61131-3 compliance
end note

:Execute Prompt 9\n**openplc-rule-checks2**\nAdditional rule checks for function\ncategorization and cleanup;
note right
  Input: Consolidated FBD from Step 8
  Output: Cleaned FBD specification
  Focus: Function vs FB categorization
end note

:Execute Prompt 10\n**append_two_inputs**\nOptimize boolean expressions\nand handle multiple inputs;
note right
  Input: Cleaned FBD from Step 9
  Output: Optimized final FBD
  Focus: Boolean minimization
end note

:Output: Complete OpenPLC\nFunction Block Diagram;
note right
  Final deliverable:
  - Function Blocks
  - Variables  
  - Functions
  - Data Connections
  - Parameter Data Connections
end note

stop

legend right
  |= Phase |= Steps |
  | Identification | Steps 1-2 |
  | Connection Logic | Steps 3-4 |
  | Parameter Config | Steps 5-6 |
  | Validation & Optimization | Steps 7-10 |
endlegend

@enduml